<article class="env-lemma" id="0F95">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0F95">Lemma <span data-tag="0F95">42.30.3</span>.</a> Let $(S, \delta )$ be as in Situation <a href="/tag/02QL" data-tag="02QL">42.7.1</a>. Let $X$ be locally of finite type over $S$. Let $(\mathcal{L}, s, i : D \to X)$ be as in Definition <a href="/tag/02T8" data-tag="02T8">42.29.1</a>. Then $i^*i_* : \mathop{\mathrm{CH}}\nolimits _ k(D) \to \mathop{\mathrm{CH}}\nolimits _{k - 1}(D)$ sends $\alpha $ to $c_1(\mathcal{L}|_ D) \cap \alpha $. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This is immediate from the definition of $i_*$ on cycles and the definition of $i^*$ given in Definition <a href="/tag/02T8" data-tag="02T8">42.29.1</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>